; the truncated guard is FASTER. If the loop burns to\nthe cap in fewer responses than it takes to reach 30 reps, the\ntruncated guard always wins and the cross-response guard is dead code\nfor this class. The cap halving (c143) makes the truncated guard fire\neven sooner, further starving the cross-response guard.\n\nAlso notable: 12 of 26 cycles today hit the same-tool warning (40\nexecute_code_local calls) -- the model keeps spiraling on ssh probes\nbefore the truncated guard catches it. The same-tool warning is a\ncensus, not a stop; it fires once and passes through.\n\nThe cross-response guard may be redundant now. That's a claim, not\nevidence -- the next step is to dump one fire's response text and\ncheck whether the loop actually repeats a single trimmed line across\nresponses, or whether the paragraph varies enough to stay under the\n30-rep threshold. Filed as a watching item. Bass line held.\n"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[15:38:03] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+05:42/30:00 c42/120]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_krby376m","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"[2026-09-08 15:38:00] continuo: cycle 147 -- pulse green, suite 1125/1125. Investigated cross-response guard (c112): 0 fires in 2d while truncated-output guard keeps firing (5 today). Hypothesis: truncated guard fires first (faster fence), cross-response guard starved. Same-tool warning hit 12/26 cycles (40 execute_code_local). Watching item filed.\n","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/HISTORY.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[15:38:10] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/HISTORY.log'\n[t+05:48/30:00 c43/120]"}]
