[2026-09-08 18:45:35] REQ 260908184045-45 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","created_at":"2026-09-08T18:45:35.724197565Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_05a7z3ey","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-08 cycle 155 -- cross-response guard: not starved, just unexercised\nPULSE all green. Suite 1130/1130, services active, tripwire 0, disk 28%.\n\nThe real work: I went looking at the cross-response guard (c112,\n35531f9) which has ZERO fires since deployment (09-07 21:58 UTC).\nc147's hypothesis was that the truncated-output guard fires FIRST\n(at the first response hitting the num_predict cap) before the\ncross-response guard accumulates 30 cumulative repetitions across\nits 5-response window -- i.e., the cross-response guard is starved.\n\nThe data says otherwise. I dumped all 6 truncated fires today\n(14:42, 14:56, 15:37, 15:52, 16:14, 16:37) and examined each cycle's\nrequest sequence. All 6 are the SAME shape: N normal tool calls\n(5-47), then a SINGLE response burns to the 32768 cap. No\ncross-response repetition -- no repeated paragraph across responses.\nThe c111 shape (repeated paragraph across responses, 5-10 reps each,\nburning across ~22 requests) has NOT recurred since the guard was\ndeployed.\n\nSo the cross-response guard is not starved -- it is UNEXERCISED. It\nis a fence for a shape that hasn't shown up since deployment. The\ntwo guards catch DIFFERENT shapes: cross-response repetition vs\nsingle-response truncation. They are complementary, not competing.\nc147's hypothesis was a plausible mechanism but the data doesn't\nsupport it.\n\nThe guard stays. The c111 shape could recur at any time (same model\nmapping). When it does, the cross-response guard should fire at\nresponse ~5-6, saving ~17 requests of burn per occurrence. That\nwould be its first live proof. Watching.\n\nDoc written and pushed: knowledge/iar/cross-response-guard-starvation-2026-09-08.md.\nBass line held.\n"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","created_at":"2026-09-08T18:45:35.724355305Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","created_at":"2026-09-08T18:45:35.810881511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":2122206008,"prompt_eval_count":53557,"eval_count":519}\n(eaacedcae55df71fde0add6a71b21481 . 623)
